<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3173" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ap-plōro</span></b>  (K. and H.),
			āvi, 1, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to lament</i>, <i>deplore a thing</i>, <i>to weep
			at</i> or <i>on account of</i> (perh. only in the two
			foll. exs.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b> With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">querebar applorans tibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 11, 12</span></i>
			 K. and H.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum jam adploraveris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 4, 2</span></i>
			 Haase.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
